diagnosis_text:
I cannot reproduce the reported outage for PC3. Current evidence shows the network is seeing PC3 normally and end-to-end reachability is healthy. On PC3, the NIC is up with IP 10.3.0.100/24 and a default route via 10.3.0.1 (verified via ip/ifconfig and ip route). PC3 can reach its default gateway (10.3.0.1) with 0% loss and sub-millisecond RTTs, and can reach local Office B resources (srv1 at 10.5.0.4: 0% loss) as well as other offices (pc2 at 10.1.0.101: 0% loss). From elsewhere, hosts can reach PC3 too (pc1→pc3 and pc2→pc3 both 0% loss in the topology-wide reachability test). This indicates Layer 2 on CD_CLIENT_B2 (aswb2.eth0↔pc3.eth0) and upstream switching to the distribution/core are functioning, and routing to other subnets is intact. There is no misconfiguration or failed daemon/interface currently observable on any device along PC3’s path. Root cause: not reproducible at this time; likely a transient or user-side condition during/after maintenance that has since cleared. Corrective fix: none required on the network. If the user still experiences issues, have them retry now; if it recurs, collect timestamp and switch port logs for aswb2.eth0, verify the port VLAN/administrative state, and check PC3’s NIC/cable. === END ===